<title>GERMANY: EMI chief - good progress in Spain, Italy, Portugal.</title>
<headline>EMI chief - good progress in Spain, Italy, Portugal.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Monetary Institute (EMI) President Alexandre Lamfalussy said on Tuesday that significant progress towards EMU had been made by Spain, Italy and Portugal.</p>
<p>Responding to a question on the chances of the so-called &quot;Club Med&quot; countries of Italy, Spain and Portugal qualifying for European currency union, Lamfalussy said the countries had made &quot;significant progress&quot;.</p>
<p>Lamfalussy was speaking to a news conference to mark the launch of the European Central Bank forerunner's third annual report.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
